WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.650
By the end of this module you should be able to
compose

00:00:02.662 --> 00:00:09.112
Boolean conditions explain SQL's three-valued logic
and handle missing values deliberately You

00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:12.575
will learn when to use IS NULL IS TRUE IS FALSE IS

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.338
UNKNOWN and IS DISTINCT FROM You will use COALESCE
for fallback logic

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.762
and NULLIF for normalization and safe ratios You
will build searched and

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:26.075
simple CASE expressions with clear boundaries and
explicit handling of missing values

00:00:26.962 --> 00:00:30.575
Finally you will combine these tools in realistic
rules and explain why

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:35.838
each row was included excluded or classified These
are reasoning skills rather

00:00:35.862 --> 00:00:40.300
than memorization tasks If you understand why the
query behaves as it

00:00:40.325 --> 00:00:43.562
does adapting it to a new dataset becomes much
easier
